inister Benjamin Netanyahu and his allies.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Swiss researchers use AI to detect early warning signs of natural disasters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2724794db22dc63e6c55ec9f174198848b2416fae700473a8842d1e38e11c156</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-swiss-researchers-use-ai-to-detect-early-warning-signs-of-natural-disasters--ded7f1a9699b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260912-swiss-researchers-use-ai-to-detect-early-warning-signs-of-natural-disasters" /><summary type="html">Scientists have long warned of more intense extreme weather events in the decades to come due to our fast-warming climate. The question they are asking is how we are going to be better prepared as we become more prone to natural disasters.A group of researchers in Switzerland believe that artificial intelligence modeling could revolutionise forecasting systems.</summary></entry><entry><title>French police suspect Normandy train derailment was result of sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2f969b9b47b21f282ec95eec66a040264ce6e5815b7022476bb67b671cb29ec</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:48:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment--ddcadeb5d26c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment" /><summary type="html">A police source said Saturday that French investigators suspect sabotage caused a train derailment in northwest France after a fragment of rail was found on the track. At least 44 people were injured in the derailment that occurred a day earlier, including an 18-year-old woman "in a critical condition".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says unified Ireland ‘would be fantastic' during Dublin trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02b8ac83ddd5f20cdc8ec9e77f086fe64127d56b9d18c2a3b80f76ad5ee62958</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:51:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament--fbbff38c8ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said a unified Ireland would be “fantastic" during a weekend visit to a major tournament at his Irish golf course. The two-day trip to Ireland is the latest example of how the US leader blends his official duties with his personal interests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS leaders gather in India as wars and US tensions test unity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f27855f385717bcaa0b2e314bae7674d6a8745cc38ad252105ee7d331ced8faf</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260912-brics-summit-set-to-be-dominated-by-wars-in-ukraine-and-iran--19071f618e81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260912-brics-summit-set-to-be-dominated-by-wars-in-ukraine-and-iran" /><summary type="html">BRICS leaders are meeting in New Delhi on Saturday to discuss trade, investment and global conflicts. The summit comes as wars in Ukraine and the Middle East, along with rising US-China tensions, test the bloc’s unity and ambitions for a greater role in global affairs.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion poised for emotional comeback concert in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78c5518b742a114378cb67b0cf2a2c4da5a6e8807e18a0fecc7755e32e64a42b</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:23:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-a-legend-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris--d2f545b260c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-a-legend-celine-dion-poised-for-emotional-comeback-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Céline Dion is set to return to the stage in Paris on Saturday for her first full concert in six years, capping a years-long battle with a rare autoimmune disorder and marking a major milestone in the Canadian superstar’s comeback.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Saudi Arabia shuts down critical oil pipeline after attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea4cdb762ab8f9931997d199d0921392f6981094bd2187b9b46307d0027dd4c9</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-live-saudi-arabia-oil-pipeline-shut-down-after-drone-attack-launched-from-iraq--7ddf3d05e286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-live-saudi-arabia-oil-pipeline-shut-down-after-drone-attack-launched-from-iraq" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia on Saturday said that it has shut down its East-West pipeline as a precaution after multiple attacks on the vital oil conduit earlier this week. Both Baghdad and Riyadh said the attacks originated in Iraqi territory, where Iranian-backed militias operate. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Children die in a school fire in Bukavu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02efcb9d647e536c97ccbf4e4c08c7457876ae6cebef0ffacaf75a4030d2fe20</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T20:18:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260911-children-die-in-a-school-fire-in-bukavu--f4db6b01d2b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260911-children-die-in-a-school-fire-in-bukavu" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme we begin in the east of the Democratic Republic of Congo, where children have died after a school fire broke out in the M23 rebel occupied city of Bukavu. Also, Senegal looks to the skies as it seeks to develop its home-grown satellite industry. And finally, we wonder about the future of African cities. How will they cope with the population boom and climate crisis? A question, the Kenya architecture biennale in Nairobi tried to answer.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthis seize near control of vital Bab el-Mandeb shipping lane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0cc2fa3757dc50d11ebc456ac6b96d9159bc29af546173a786000a3d050da80</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T20:09:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane--31b17fb442d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-iran-backed-houthis-seize-near-control-of-vital-bab-el-mandeb-shipping-lane" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels captured the strategic Perim Island in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, located at the southern entrance to the Red Sea, officials said on Friday. The lightning move opens a new front in the Iran war and threatens energy supplies, especially Saudi oil exports, from passing through one of the world's key shipping lanes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Saudi shuts East-West oil pipeline after multiple Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa6a4e4daa4538aa3de3675cf9e7499ede432d5495816944eebff01cab89fcc9</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T19:25:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran--68a101e1037f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges Trump to impose new Russia sanctions 'now', after deadly Ukraine strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fe874498df75cca3352cc16788e44f06e9aff1c6d46e9f36ccf6f960f181725</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:15:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T19:13:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes--228fa885e3a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday urged US President Donald Trump to impose new sanctions on Russia over deadly strikes on Ukraine, as Kyiv and Moscow step up attacks and US-led efforts to end the war remain deadlocked.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Can we slowdown AI, and 9/11, who has the right to remember?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4f7462d02a8c5b1c6bb9d0ea3c89fca900cc76ab219f7ff85567fed641c9caf</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T18:43:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember--b55b74262dd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember" /><summary type="html">In a week that marks 25 years since 9/11, Americans paused to pay tribute. Six bells tolled to signify six fatal moments in New York, at the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania, with a seventh bell rung this year to commemorate those who later died from 9/11-related illnesses.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Spotlight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0279cb9fe742a85ff7a34ee7d2238daa6c7ea452872761c213d9df9cd47a34be</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T18:42:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight--86e38a56a856.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight" /><summary type="html">The New York Times reporter Carol Rosenberg is widely regarded as one of the foremost American journalists, if not the foremost, on the U.S. detention camp at Guantanamo Bay in Cuba, where several alleged suspects in the 9/11 attacks are still being held, including the alleged “architect” of the attacks, alongside three other suspected plotters.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro probed for corruption as Brazil election tightens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2973d9dc3f687c09302aeaf59896605d2a538c3c22a3d1a3fb97a128bf357ceb</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T16:21:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-flavio-bolsonaro-probed-for-corruption-as-brazil-election-tightens--7d6742f29229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-flavio-bolsonaro-probed-for-corruption-as-brazil-election-tightens" /><summary type="html">Just weeks before the vote, Brazilian presidential hopeful Flavio Bolsonaro's campaign is being rocked by revelations he is under investigation for alleged corruption and money laundering. The probe centres on financing sought for a film about his father, former president Jair Bolsonaro, court documents unsealed on Friday showed.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Elections in Russia: the 1001 tricks to remove inconvenient candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e44c21f04dab51a660c1b3e35989968fab77a40b8e07d6364d6395ef12e23690</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T16:11:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates--c49abd54b7c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates" /><summary type="html">The Russian authorities are using dubious claims to disqualify candidates previously cleared to run in the parliamentary election from September 18 to 20. The war in Ukraine is making the Kremlin even more cautious about who is allowed to campaign.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump delivers remarks at Pentagon ceremony to mark 25th anniversary of 9/11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a345ffa914221305fbe24b455a2261e66c809a68d4bb36e300601d26efec960</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-trump-delivers-remarks-at-pentagon-ceremony-to-mark-25th-anniversary-of-9-11--e6337c0b2900.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-trump-delivers-remarks-at-pentagon-ceremony-to-mark-25th-anniversary-of-9-11" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump observed Friday’s 25th anniversary by speaking about 9/11 at a ceremony at the Pentagon commemorating the lives lost when al-Qaeda militants hijacked planes and killed nearly 3,000 people in three locations, upending American foreign policy and national security.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Chaos and a sense of doom': Memories of 9/11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4329727b97259df9a7da33f7bb9e8baf08c3e1327a4e121c83c662da9eb3676</id><updated>2026-09-12T12:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:20:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-chaos-and-a-sense-of-doom-memories-of-9-11--6a2e907edd0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-chaos-and-a-sense-of-doom-memories-of-9-11" /><summary type="html">Dulcie Leimbach, editor and co-founder of PassBlue, was a journalist in New York working for the New York Times at the time of the September 11 terror attacks. She shared her memories of that day with France 24. "I saw bodies falling from the North Tower," she recalls.</summary></entry></feed>
